comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T23:39:08.070Z",codex-sol,"Restart review clarification: ae65f73 deliberately changes installed-extension responses to extensionAvailable=false and the built-in pm-web neighbors shape (center plus one-hop incoming/outgoing neighbors). Safe GET/HEAD no longer activates pm-graph or returns its native payload. No version field was introduced. Existing extension-native response parity is NOT proven or marked met; that acceptance remains open under related pm-web-38n5. Real graph regression proves the built-in shape and security boundary, not extension-native parity. Preserve four-metric coverage and independent review/deployment prerequisites."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T17:09:23.503Z",codex,"TDD: the existing neighbor route failed the new real HTTP/PostgreSQL/PM workspace test because it returned no center and activated extensions for a viewer. The observational fallback now returns one-hop outgoing and incoming relationships, a null center for missing or other-project node IDs, and leaves extension settings/install/marker untouched. Focused test passes. Typecheck, lint, and 0%-clone gate also pass; full release gate and exact-head review remain pending."
  "2026-09-26T17:19:15.048Z",codex,"Final observational neighbors implementation: GET/HEAD uses fallbackGraphForProject (SDK certified complete-list read with noExtensions), returns one-hop outgoing/incoming data, missing nodes as null, and isolates a second project. Real HTTP/PostgreSQL/PM marker-extension regression failed before change and now passes as linked test 1/1. npm run release:check exits 0: 409/409 tests, 0 skipped, 0 clone pairs across 142 TS sources, 600 documented declarations, 0 production audit vulnerabilities, packed npm/Bun acceptance. Measured overall source coverage 84.39% lines, 80.48% branches, 77.82% functions, below the user’s 100% target. pm health strict ok=true with 2 stale-item advisories. Hosted deployment and exact-head bot review remain pending."
